# Shell scripts MUST check out with LF, on every platform.
#
# `scripts/verify-linux*.sh` run inside a Linux container. A CRLF checkout — which is what
# this repository gets on Windows, where `core.autocrlf` is true — makes bash read every line
# as ending in a literal carriage return: `$'\r': command not found`, on the first line.
#
# It worked when written only because the file was created with LF and never round-tripped
# through a checkout. A fresh clone would have broken it, which is the kind of failure that
# shows up for the next person and not for the author.
*.sh text eol=lf
